<title>JAPAN: Fannie Mae launches $500 mln 5-yr global bonds.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae launches $500 mln 5-yr global bonds.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal National Mortgage Association (Fannie Mae) launched $500 million worth of five-year global bonds due January 16, 2002, Merrill Lynch, one of the lead managers, said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bonds will be priced 10 basis points above the yield of five-year U.S. Treasury notes.  </p>
<p>Merrill Lynch said the price negotations will be held during New York trading hours later today.</p>
<p>The payment date will be on January 16, it said.</p>
<p>The other lead manager is Lehman Brothers.</p>
</text>
